## Why nougat was not run

- Model equations are well-formed and unambiguous in `pdftotext -layout` output
  (verified by verbatim transcription into `scripts/smoke_belov2015.py`).
- Tables A.1 and A.2 render cleanly in the text extraction; no mathematical
  formula parsing failures encountered.
- Nougat's marginal value would be in preserving equation typography (LaTeX form)
  and multi-column layout; neither was needed here.
- LUCID-100 slot 66 is B-tier (rank 97); GPU compute was reserved for higher-tier
  slots and slots with formula-heavy PDFs where pdftotext fails.

## When to promote this stub to a real nougat parse

- If a downstream tool (e.g. an LLM-based equation verifier) needs LaTeX-form
  equations rather than plain-text ones.
- If the K1..K7 units question (see `report/failure_analysis.md` §1.1) requires
  formal MathML / LaTeX to disambiguate the exponents.
- If the JTB paywalled version is obtained and diff'd against the JINR preprint
  at the equation-symbol level.

## Reproducer (if promoting to real parse)

```bash
# on a GPU host (uicgpu A100 or Polaris)
pip install nougat-ocr
nougat artifacts/belov2015_inis_iaea.pdf -o extraction/ --model 0.1.0-base --markdown
# → extraction/belov2015_inis_iaea.mmd (this file, replaced)
```

Expected wall-clock: ~2–5 min on a single A100 for a 35-page paper.

